mynote =       {\enquote{Thermodynamics is a comparatively old science, and is universally recognized as one of the fundamental subjects in chemical engineering. In spite of this, much of the fundamental research which has been carried out on the foundations of thermodynamics in the last twenty years has been largely ignored by the chemical engineering community, and thermodynamics is still being thaught, used and referred to in chemical engineering essentially along traditional lines, and according to concepts and vaguely stated rules which have been shown to be wrong or, at best, valid only under limiting conditions. (Here and in the following, we refer for simplicity only to chemical engineering, though most of the arguments developed apply, in our opinion, also more generally to chemistry, and particularly to industrial chemistry).} p.~680}
