mynote =       {\enquote{Perhaps it is trite to observe that statements about confidence levels are conditional on the assumptions made, but this fact is often ignored in ``applied'' circles. This note is written to ventilate this issue. The key criticisms are that the assumptions invoked are frequently gratuitous and, more damaging, that the procedures often are not robust with respect to departures from these assumptions.} \enquote{Perhaps the reason for the susceptibility to invoking assumptions of doubtful validity is a preoccupation with making ``objective'' statements. Ironically, the practical relevance of these statements depends on the ``closeness'' of the assumptions to reality, which must be \emph{subjectively} assessed. Certainly in the examples mentioned, the writer would prefer to proceed in a frankly subjective manner, taking account of any extrastatistical information available.}}
}

