year =         {2017},
volume =       {3},
series =       {The Stormlight Archive},
address =      {New York},
mynote =       {\enquote{I don't need \emph{company} to be \emph{confident}}, Jasnah, \chap38. \enquote{\emph{You} decide how you are defined. Don't surrender that to them. They will gleefully take the chance to define you, if you allow it.}, Jasnah, \chap38. \enquote{It becomes the responsibility of every man, upon realizing he lacks the truth, to seek it out. --From \emph{The Way of Kings}, postscript} \chap121. \begin{quotation}The most important words a man can say are, ``I will do better.'' These are not the most important words \emph{any} man can say. I am a man, and they are what I needed to say.\par The ancient code of the Knights Radiant says ``journey before destination.'' Some may call it a simple platitude, but it is far more. A journey will have pain and failure. It is not only the steps forward that we must accept. It is the stumbles. The trials. The knowledge that we will fail. That we will hurt those around us.\par But if we stop, if we accept the person we are when we fall, the journey ends. That failure \emph{becomes} our destination.\par To love the journey is to accept no such end. I have found, through painful experience, that the most important step a person can take is always the \emph{next} one.\par I'm certain some will feel threatened by this record. Some few may feel liberated. Most will simply feel that it should not exist.\par I needed to write it anyway.\end{quotation} Dalinar Kholin \chap122}
